Help - RetroOS Executable Help
------------------------------
Available commands (simulated):

help.exe
  Shows this help text.

hello_world.exe
  Prints a "Hello World" message.

cool_app.exe
  Simulated application startup messages.

sysinfo.exe
  Displays system information (CPU, Memory, Drives).

ping.exe [host]
  Simulates pinging a host. Example: ping.exe example.local

calc.exe [expression]
  Performs simple calculations. Example: calc.exe "2 + 2"

dirlist.exe [path]
  Lists a simulated directory. Example: dirlist.exe C:\\

echo.exe [text]
  Echoes the provided text back.

Notes:
- These are harmless text-based placeholders. Some accept arguments in their text output to demonstrate interactivity, but the demo primarily streams static file contents.
- To add a new executable, place a plain-text file in retro-startup/reference/executables/ and add the filename to manifest.json.
